{"name":"Circus Red","hex":"#954a4c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"circus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A traveling company of performers that may include acrobats, clowns, trained animals, and other novelty acts, that gives shows usually in a circular tent. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A round open space in a town or city where multiple streets meet."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take part in a circus; or to be displayed as if in a circus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/circus"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Circus","blocks":[{"text":"A circus is a company of performers who put on diverse entertainment shows that may include clowns, acrobats, trained animals, trapeze acts, musicians, dancers, hoopers, tightrope walkers, jugglers, magicians, ventriloquists, and unicyclists as well as other object manipulation and stunt-oriented artists. The term \"circus\" also describes the field of performance, training, and community which has followed various formats through its 250-year modern history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Barnum_%26_Bailey_clowns_and_geese2.jpg/330px-Barnum_%26_Bailey_clowns_and_geese2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circus"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Champion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg/500px-Champion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Champion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg/500px-Champion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sells Brothers Circus with Great Danes ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChampion_great_danes_from_the_Imperial_kennels%2C_poster_for_Forepaugh_and_Sells_Brothers%2C_1898.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Astley%27s_Amphitheatre_Microcosm_edited.jpg/500px-Astley%27s_Amphitheatre_Microcosm_edited.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Astley%27s_Amphitheatre_Microcosm_edited.jpg/500px-Astley%27s_Amphitheatre_Microcosm_edited.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki